rewind-assets reads Counter-Strike 2 files from the user's own installation at runtime.
No Valve game content is included in this repository or in Rewind's builds.

Third-party work this crate builds on:

* heatel 0.1.0 (MIT, https://github.com/alexstanovoy/heatel), vendored in crates/vendor/heatel
  with patches marked "REWIND PATCH" (CS2 compressed-mip-size entries, zstd mips, per-level
  decoding, level dropping). heatel itself credits ValveResourceFormat (see its
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES).

* ValveResourceFormat / Source 2 Viewer (MIT, https://github.com/ValveResourceFormat/ValveResourceFormat):
  the world node / aggregate fragment / LoD mask / layer rules (WorldNodeLoader.cs,
  SceneAggregate.cs, ModelLodInfo.cs) and the material blend/overlay rules
  (ShaderDataProvider.cs) were ported from it.

